    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Note: Reinhardt's \"Last paintings\" and Sugimoto's\nseascape photographs are not \"monochromes\" in the strictest\nsense, though they would look uniformly black\nto the casual glance of a passer-by. These pieces demand a very active\nkind of observation, which reveals\n(very simple) patterns, created by different tones of black. The ambiguity\nwhich constitutes their perceptual essence is impossible\nto reproduce through a small-scale image on a computer screen. Nonetheless,\nthey cannot be skipped in this anthology.",
      "links": []
    },
